### The one structural change: this stack now serves TWO consumers

Until 2026-09-05 every capacity figure here was defended against one consumer at a measured peak of 2.
That is no longer the shape of the problem.

| consumer | what it is | its own limit |
|---|---|---|
| `deepseek-harness` | the agentic harness, via `MESSAGE.md` | `maxConcurrentAgents: 8` |
| `eda-mastra-platform` | OpenWebUI + Mastra + docling/whisper sidecars | steady 2, burst 4, schedulable harness runs |

**Both bind to `chat-model` at 131,072 and to `embedding-model` at 2560 dims.** The second consumer
holds a standing GPU reservation — see §2d — which is why util is 0.64 and seats are 8. **Do not
reclaim that free card memory.** It is not slack; it is docling and faster-whisper, and it was
measured and committed, not estimated.

The foundry has no session in this repo. It is reached by cross-session message, and its questions do
**not** belong in `MESSAGE.md`, which is the harness channel by definition. Conclusions from either
consumer still go in `docs/TUNING.md`.

