### Validate fp8 KV — the exact procedure

fp8 KV halves per-token cost, so the same `0.70` would hold **8** sessions at 131,072 instead of 4
(4.17 GiB per full-context sequence instead of 8.33). `Qwen3.8-27B-FP8` ships **no** `kv_cache_scheme`,
so `auto` gives it bf16 and forcing fp8 means uncalibrated dynamic scales — numerics unmeasured on
this checkpoint. The grid already supports the experiment (`scripts/eval-grid.sh:181`,
`export KV_CACHE_DTYPE="${KV_EVAL_DTYPE:-bfloat16}"`):

```bash
./scripts/preflight.sh                           # asserts --kv-cache-dtype accepts fp8 (no GPU cost)
# NOTE: this mv was NEVER RUN. The bf16 baseline is still at results/eval/, and README.md and this
# file now cite it there. If you do run it, re-point those citations in the same commit.
mv results/eval results/eval-bf16-20260820       # cells at a different KV dtype are NOT peers
docker compose down                              # the grid needs the card to itself
./scripts/run-detached.sh kvfp8 env KV_EVAL_DTYPE=fp8 EFFORTS=off,medium \
  ./scripts/eval-grid.sh fp8

# Watch it. BOTH variables are needed: grid-status.sh defaults to the tmux session `kb-grid` and
# the full 8-cell matrix, so without them it reports this run as "not running", shows six
# permanently `pending` rows, and `-w` never exits because 2 cells can never reach 8.
GRID_SESSION=kvfp8 ARMS=fp8 EFFORTS=off,medium ./scripts/grid-status.sh -w
```

**Two corrections to the command this section used to give, both made 2026-08-20 before running it.**
It read `env KV_EVAL_DTYPE=fp8 EFFORTS=off,medium ARMS=fp8`, and two-thirds of that was inert:

- `EFFORTS=off,medium` **was silently ignored.** `eval-grid.sh` reassigned `EFFORTS=(off low medium
  xhigh)` unconditionally, so the "two cells, ~1 h" run would have been four cells at roughly four
  times the wall clock, with the provenance recording the default it actually used. `EFFORTS` is now
  read from the environment with the same defaulting discipline as `MAXTOK`, comma or space
  separated, and an unknown value is **refused** — a cell directory is named `<arm>-<effort>`, so a
  typo would create a cell `collect-results.py` cannot place and the grid would look complete while
  missing a row. Same failure class as the variable-prefix trap in `run-detached.sh`'s header: the
  tunable arrives correctly and the script overwrites it.
- `ARMS=fp8` as an environment variable does nothing and never did — `ARMS` comes from the
  **positional** arguments (`ARMS=("${@:-nvfp4 fp8}")`), which the trailing `fp8` already supplies.
  Harmless, but it implied a knob that is not there.

A **third** fault surfaced on the first launch, from the cell's own provenance rather than from
reading code: the run booted at `util 0.70 / max-num-seqs 12` against a baseline recorded at
`0.92 / 20`. `.env` was being sourced into the grid's environment and overriding the script's shape
defaults — see the added paragraph under Resume. The run was killed ~5 minutes in, the leak was
closed, and the relaunch boots at `0.92 / 40960 / 20`, matching
`results/eval/fp8-off/provenance.txt` (NOT `results/eval-bf16-20260820/` — that rename never
happened) in every field except `--kv-cache-dtype`. That is
the point of the experiment: **one** variable. Check it the same way before trusting any cell —
`diff` the new provenance against the archived one and require the KV dtype to be the only
difference.

`preflight.sh` now also asserts `--kv-cache-dtype` accepts `fp8` and `bfloat16`, not just `auto`, so
a value the image no longer takes fails in a no-GPU-cost check rather than at engine boot — after the
production stack has already been taken down for the experiment.

Two cells, ~1 h. Archiving first is not optional: the KV dtype is part of the cell fingerprint, so
the grid **refuses** to mix them and `collect-results.py` would otherwise have two generations to
tabulate. Compare against the committed baseline — `fp8/off` mean 87.6, `fp8/medium` 89.6 — and accept
only if the gap sits inside the ≤1.7-point bound the paired test already established for this task
mix. ~~If it holds: set `KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8` and `CHAT_MAX_NUM_SEQS=8` in `.env`.~~ **DEAD — do not
follow.** Three things are wrong with it: the session count went 8 → 7 → 5 → **4** on measured
co-residency (`docs/TUNING.md` 3); `KV_CACHE_DTYPE` is the *shared* variable, and setting it
downgrades the nvfp4 arm's calibrated static scales (`docs/TUNING.md` 5) — the per-arm
`KV_CACHE_DTYPE_FP8` is what shipped; and the gate is `./scripts/shape.sh`, not a hardcoded number.

**Re-derive `request_timeout` as part of any session-count change, not after it.** More sessions
means slower per-stream decode under saturation, so the full-output term grows and can pass the
configured timeout. Re-run `./scripts/measure-ttft.py --streams N` on the new shape and take the
`inter_token_latency_seconds` mean from its saturated leg; the arithmetic is in `litellm/config.yaml`
above `request_timeout`.

